# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 4 (a function of a block reads the block's names), ch. 8 (a widget applied is transparent; one that calls itself builds as deep as its data) and ruling TC (places are counted as built): three levels each build their label, the last arm builds "ground", and the block's label takes the next number; the click moves the three labels that read $count, in its own tick. Never run.
test t

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Button(label="add")
    1: Ui.Label(text="level 2 at 0")
    2: Ui.Label(text="level 1 at 0")
    3: Ui.Label(text="level 0 at 0")
    4: Ui.Label(text="ground")
    5: Ui.Label(text="after")

tick 1
  in:
    0: click
  changed:
    1: Ui.Label(text="level 2 at 1")
    2: Ui.Label(text="level 1 at 1")
    3: Ui.Label(text="level 0 at 1")
